-- Plane selection: every unrefuted consensus edge whose relation type belongs
-- to the given salience band, strongest (eff_mu) first. This is the primitive
-- the foundry/synthesis and band-scoped readers should use instead of hand-rolled
-- rank-threshold scans.
--
-- Native (highway_mask.c): the band's relation-type id set is computed
-- entirely in memory from the highway perfcache (bit -> canonical -> type id,
-- zero DB round trips), then ONE indexed query fetches the edges
-- (consensus_type_btree for the ANY() filter, the eff_mu expression index for
-- ordering) — the define_fast pattern.
-- NO DROP. `DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS consensus.band_edges(int, bigint, bigint)`
-- stood here and broke EVERY extension upgrade (2026-08-11 06:38, migrate phase):
--
--   ERROR: cannot drop function consensus.band_edges(integer,bigint,bigint)
--          because other objects depend on it
--   DETAIL: function ops.band_leaders(integer[],integer) depends on it
--
-- ops.band_leaders is `LANGUAGE sql STABLE BEGIN ATOMIC`, and an ATOMIC body is
-- parsed at CREATE time and records a real pg_depend edge on everything it
-- references (that is the whole point of the form, and why the G12 gate — string
-- SQL bodies, GH #764 — pushes toward it). So converting a caller to ATOMIC
-- retroactively turns any DROP of its callees into an upgrade-blocking error,
-- and the manifest installs band_edges before band_leaders — the dependent from
-- the PREVIOUS install is still present when the DROP runs.
--
-- The DROP was redundant anyway: name, argument types and return type are all
-- unchanged, so CREATE OR REPLACE alone does the job. A DROP is only load-bearing
-- when the signature or return type CHANGES; this one bought nothing and cost the
-- whole deploy. Same class as #1004, which removed ten of these under identity/.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION consensus.band_edges(
    p_band       int,
    p_min_eff_mu bigint DEFAULT NULL,
    p_limit      bigint DEFAULT 1000)
    RETURNS TABLE(
        subject_id    bytea,
        type_id       bytea,
        object_id     bytea,
        rating        bigint,
        rd            bigint,
        witness_count bigint,
        eff_mu        bigint)
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_consensus_band_edges'
    LANGUAGE C STABLE;
